 "scoring_plan": [
  "Target: the first Pew Research Center American Trends Panel, annual trust-in-science survey (web, with some phone since late 2024; 5,111 U.S. adults in 2025, the scientists item asked of a random half) release of the item quoted in study.item from its next wave (fieldwork expected from 2026-10-19), Pew Research Center's published figures.",
  "Not scored, with the reason, if Pew Research Center does not ask the item in that wave, changes its wording or answer options, published the wave before this seal's OpenTimestamps attestation, or has not published it by 2027-05-13.",
  "Share: great deal or fair amount, the printed percentage of 'A great deal of confidence' plus 'A fair amount of confidence' (Pew prints 'No answer' (web skips and phone refusals, <1 or 1 percent) in the topline and keeps it in the base. The headline is Pew's printed NET (great deal plus fair amount, computed by Pew from unrounded data), taken as printed, not rescaled; it can differ by a point from the sum of the printed parts.). Total: the topline. Cells: the published group each cut in study.cells maps to; a group the release does not publish is not scored.",
  "Metric: absolute miss in points, for the forecast and for both sealed baselines. Headline = the total. Beside it: the mean over the 3 exactly mapped cells. Printed integers carry up to half a point of rounding per printed figure.",
  "Bands: whether each published share falls inside the sealed 80% and 95% bands.",
  "Claim: 'sealed before fieldwork' only if the wave's published fieldwork start is later than the attestation's block time; otherwise 'sealed before publication'."
 ]
